        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(agents): enforce computer-use policy in Claude CLI runtime",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nClaude CLI sessions could receive OpenClaw-managed MCP servers, including computer-use, but the generic CLI path could not enforce OpenClaw's effective per-tool policy before native Claude MCP calls reached the upstream server. This made direct computer-use integration incomplete and left Claude's own permission settings as a separate enforcement surface.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis change promotes the existing `claude-stdio` transport into a persistent runtime-like path while keeping `claude-cli` correctly modeled as a `CliBackend`. OpenClaw-managed external MCP servers are routed through an OpenClaw-owned proxy that filters discovery, applies the effective global/provider/agent/group/sender/sandbox policy, relays pre/post tool hooks, preserves native backend-owned MCP entries, and supports stdio, HTTP/SSE, and WebSocket upstreams.\n\nThe reserved Claude server name `computer-use` is rewritten only in the generated launch config. OpenClaw policy continues to use the configured server identity, and Claude's native computer-use namespace is explicitly disabled so calls cannot bypass the managed proxy.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can use an OpenClaw-managed computer-use MCP server with `agentRuntime.id: \"claude-cli\"` and a narrow `toolFilter`. Claude sees only allowed tools, every forwarded operation is authorized by OpenClaw first, and follow-up turns retain the same sender/auth context and live runtime session.\n\nNative backend `--mcp-config` entries remain Claude-owned and byte-preserved unless an OpenClaw-managed server intentionally replaces the same identity.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 504 focused tests passed across agent CLI, gateway MCP, follow-up context, hook relay, policy proxy, and spawned Claude e2e surfaces.\n- Fresh autoreview reported no actionable findings (`patch is correct`, confidence `0.84`).\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwq1tchh08ha6d6p47fgff4v` passed `pnpm check:changed`, the Linux spawned-Claude MCP e2e, and `pnpm build`.\n- Testbox Actions run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28713605711\n- Local Claude Code version: `2.1.152`.\n- A live `list_apps` request reached the computer-use MCP path but timed out against the machine's pre-existing shared CUA client state. No unrelated shared processes were terminated, so an actual desktop action remains the known live-proof gap.\n\nAI-assisted implementation. I reviewed the architecture, code, tests, and validation results.\n",
